      "claim": "The stopping process requires an impulse equal to the initial momentum to reduce the ship's velocity to zero.",
      "evidence": "Impulse-Momentum Theorem: $\\Delta p = F_{avg} \\Delta t$. To stop, $\\Delta p = p_{initial} - 0 = p_{initial}$.",
      "weight": 0.25,
      "depends_on": [2]
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "claim": "Assuming comparable average stopping forces, the ship with greater momentum requires a longer time to stop.",
      "evidence": "Rearranging the impulse equation to $\\Delta t = \\Delta p / F_{avg}$. If $\\Delta p$ is larger and $F_{avg}$ is approximately constant, $\\Delta t$ must be larger.",
