      "claim": "The assumption of comparable stopping forces is physically valid for 'identical' ships in the same medium.",
      "evidence": "Hydrodynamic drag is primarily a function of hull shape, surface area, and speed. While displacement changes slightly, the hull geometry (the main determinant of drag coefficient) is identical. Thus, $F_{drag}$ is comparable, making the difference in stopping time attributable to the difference in momentum/inertia rather than a drastic difference in force.",
